  "instance_name": "false_equivalence_meme_trope",
  "label": "False Equivalence Meme Trope",
  "description": "This meme uses a common internet trope of false equivalence — comparing two unrelated or incomparable things to create a misleading or humorous argument. In this case, it equates gun control (a matter of public safety and law enforcement) with TV licensing (a matter of media consumption and revenue collection), which are fundamentally different policy areas. The intent is to mock or criticize gun control policies by framing them as leading to an absurd consequence, which is a form of political satire that misrepresents complex policy decisions.",
